Metric:
- id: usage.dau_mau
- name: 
- description: The Daily-to-Monthly Active User Ratio (DAU/MAU) is a key performance indicator that measures user engagement within a business intelligence platform. This metric quantifies the proportion of users who engage with the platform on a daily basis compared to those who engage at least once in a month. A higher DAU/MAU ratio indicates that users are not only accessing the platform regularly but are also finding value in its features and insights. This stickiness metric is crucial for understanding user retention and the effectiveness of content governance strategies. By analyzing this ratio, organizations can identify trends in user behavior and make informed decisions to enhance user experience and drive deeper engagement with BI tools.

