Metric:
- id: usage.drilldown
- name: 
- description: This metric measures the proportion of user interactions that involve drill-through actions within business intelligence tools. It indicates the extent to which users engage in exploratory analysis by navigating from high-level summaries to more detailed data views. A higher proportion of drill-down interactions suggests that users are actively seeking deeper insights and are not solely relying on static reports. This behavior reflects a more dynamic use of BI content, where users are empowered to investigate underlying data trends and patterns. Monitoring this metric helps organizations understand user engagement levels and the effectiveness of their BI content in supporting informed decision-making.

