- description: This metric evaluates the extent to which self-service business intelligence (BI) tools are being adopted across the organization. It measures the number of users who actively create and share their own reports and dashboards, indicating a culture of data empowerment. Additionally, it assesses the governance structures in place to ensure that self-service practices align with organizational standards and data integrity. The metric also tracks active usage rates, reflecting how frequently these self-service tools are utilized in decision-making processes. Overall, this metric provides insights into the effectiveness of BI initiatives aimed at democratizing data access and fostering a data-driven culture.

