Metric:
- id: decision.traceability
- name: 
- description: This metric measures the extent to which decisions made within the Business Intelligence (BI) framework are connected to governed dashboards and their underlying data lineage. It assesses the clarity and accessibility of the links between decision logs and the visualizations or reports that informed those decisions. Higher traceability indicates that stakeholders can easily trace back the rationale behind decisions to specific data sources and analytical outputs. This transparency fosters trust in the decision-making process and ensures that decisions are evidence-based. The scope of this metric includes all logged decisions within the BI system, focusing on their connections to governed content and the integrity of data lineage.

